  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b366-40eb-8a0f-0617" name="Gallic (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #12 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The Gauls spread through France, Switzerland, Austria, Britain, Italy, the Balkans and Asia Minor. This list covers those tribes present in France and Italy down to the conquest of Gaul by Julius Caesar. There is some debate over the density of Gallic warbands and while the list shows them as close order troops, you may if you wish field ALL warriors and fanatic units in open order for +2 points per model – all or nothing choice! Allies: A Gallic army may take allies from the Etruscan or Italian Hill Tribes lists.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Gallic]
  Cavalry and Chariots: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Skirmishers: up to 20%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Cavalry and Chariots: Up to 25% Skirmishers: Up to 20% Allies: Up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
